% Generate pdd/cloud_server/store.py as owner-scoped SQLite persistence.

Export StoreError with status_code, JsonObject, and the storage functions used by the API.
Initialize sessions, commands, examples, and FTS5 tables idempotently.
Create the database with mode 0600, enable WAL, foreign keys, and a 15-second busy timeout.
Close connections deterministically. Use BEGIN IMMEDIATE for write transactions.
Use parameterized SQL and UTC-aware ISO timestamps.
Require session ownership before reading or modifying commands. Hide foreign state with 404.
Derive active/stale from heartbeat age. Closed sessions are excluded from listSessions.
Deregister idempotently closes the session and cancels pending/processing commands.
Preserve cancellation against late worker updates; terminal results are immutable.
Repeated identical terminal updates succeed; conflicting transitions return 409.
Registration and command submission deduplicate optional Idempotency-Key values.
Reject key reuse with changed bodies; keep keys scoped by owner or session.
Example IDs hash owner plus canonical payload. Repeated uploads do not duplicate records.
Examples are private unless metadata.isPublic is exactly true.
Shared examples remain restricted to authenticated users.
FTS5 searches owner-visible examples, supports language filtering, and returns bounded results.

